yself struggling with some social  anxiety problems like  bonnie i don't know i just i related to  her immediately immediately that she was  kind of in her own shell  and those are the kind of characters  that i like playing  so when you're saying the kind of  character you like playing when you read  a script  is there any roles that are red flag to  you that you kind of won't take  no i mean i'm down for anything i've  played all kinds of characters but  my favorite and probably because it is  some sort of catharsis you know to play  somebody who  i'm very shy and introverted as a person  and  so i tend to gravitate towards those  characters because i know eventually  they won't be  normally in a script there's a journey  for them and so then maybe on the other  side of making something i will have  gone through the same journey and will  come out of my shell a little more  that's always the goal  but yeah oh i love that that's that's an  amazing answer  so also too with this film being an  indie project  can you kind of share the pros of doing  an indie film compared to doing  something like a paranormal activity  that you did  yeah i mean indie film is always where  my heart is at it's what i love doing  the most  um most of my friends are indie  filmmakers and  i just love the camaraderie and i love  you know everybody on set  is there because they want to be and  they love it and not that that isn't the  case on larger  projects but it's not as intimate and  it's sometimes not as rewarding as a  small movie can be  and you know i think that that's why  this movie works so well is because  everybody was  just like madly in love with each other  every day on set like we had the most  fun and we're all friends in real life  so  it's i think that that kind of energy  comes across on the projects and on  screen and i think it really did with  this one  yeah and you know you also what's cool  about you is you're a huge fan of film  and tv and you always share on like your  instagram stuff you're watching  do you now when you're in something like  magicians or a movie like this  do you run and go watch yourself are you  someone you can't really watch yourself  no i hate watching myself honestly okay  um no i have definitely seen i've seen a  few seasons of magicians but um  i have not watched all of it i can't  it's mostly because like i really just  love making the thing i love  the process of making it and being on  set that's that's why i do this  um the finished product is out of my  hands so sometimes it can be  heartbreaking but  i did watch stallions and i love it so  much i love it  so freaking much it turned out really  well i think and i'm really proud of it  so  um yeah no after the last year of being  quarantined you have to stare at our  faces on screens like i'm coming  over it yeah 100 and speaking of this  like crazy last year was it  hard to like work on your craft as an  actress when you're like in lockdown can  you kind of explain that  was there like a way you were kind of  just practicing if that makes sense  no i was pretty rough i mean my  therapist was always trying to come up  with ways she's like well why don't you  get dressed up in a costume and just  like dance through his house and i'm  like i do that anyway that's why i hired  you to get me to stop doing that  i um don't it was rough honestly but  out of it came a lot of cool things i'm  working on a lot of projects with  friends that we wrote during the  pandemic and um yeah you know a lot of  really great art will come out of this  so  you mentioned stuff you wrote are you  looking to get more into writing more  things and  would you ever consider directing yeah i  have i've written  um i used to write a lot of comedy you  had a web series for a long time years  ago  so i i have written and i i did direct a  short  right before pandemic that hopefully  will come out um  and i'm producing a couple movies right  now so i'm always having my hands and  and everything but  acting is what i love but i just love  filmmaking in general  sure and you know most people are going  to know you from magicians in that  amazing character of alice you played  now that it's sad that it's come to an  end would you though in your career if  someone was to offer you like  another steady role in tv would you  still consider that are you trying to  kind of go a different path at the  moment  no i would i think television is amazing  right now and you know we're in the  golden age of television and  i've i've been reading a lot of really  wonderful scripts lately  and i'm just like wow tv is it's really  thrilling and it's nice  it's also nice to have a job a  long-running job but i'm i'm  i hope i get to do a balance of both to  be honest like i'm in vancouver right  now about to start a  small movie and i hope i get to do more  movies like stallions and  more tv shows you know sure and and you  mentioned you do so many things which is  so true  and i love that you do a cameo for  charity which i think is awesome  uh but have you gotten any crazy  requests on cameo  yeah ones i'm not even gonna say but  yeah people have had some crazy requests  for sure yeah i love doing i love  doing videos for fans it's really fun  but um  some of them i definitely don't don't  accommodate yeah  no makes sense um also too you have a  beautiful horse you always share  pictures of  on instagram when did you start writing  riding horses has this been something  your whole life  yeah i've ridden since i was like five  so i've ridden my whole life my mom rode  horses and i've shown and bred and  trained horses my whole life and then  took a long break especially while  shooting magicians and then  when the last season of magicians i was  like if this i need to get a horse again  i need something that's not just work  and um yeah actually it's been a a major  savior during this past year is that the  only place i would go is the barn so  yeah love w